  "label": "Baby is doing the dishes",
  "description": "The text 'dss' (an acronym for 'doing the dishes') is overlaid on the image and humorously maps onto the visual of the baby interacting with the open dishwasher. The meme implies that the baby is performing the adult household chore of doing the dishes, creating an absurd and infantilizing analogy. This mapping relies on the juxtaposition of the baby's innocent appearance (shirtless, in a diaper) with the adult task, reinforcing the joke through visual-textual alignment.",
